  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100959,
      "id": "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc",
      "title": "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "265f9832-06dd-5e07-afcd-deac07c6479a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 4 y \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)},\\,\\cos(4 x)\\ne0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=1 - 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$\n- **II.** $y=2 - 2 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$\n- **III.** $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=1 - 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=12 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 4 y \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ 12 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\overset{?}{=}-4\\cdot \\left(1 - 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\tan\\left(4 x\\right) \\\\ 12 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\overset{?}{=}12 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 4 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ 4 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=1 - 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 - 2 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 4 y \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ 8 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\overset{?}{=}-4\\cdot \\left(2 - 2 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\tan\\left(4 x\\right) \\\\ 8 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\overset{?}{=}8 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 8 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ 8 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 - 2 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 4 y \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\overset{?}{=}-4\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\tan\\left(4 x\\right) \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\overset{?}{=}- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 4 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ 4 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
